// arXiv source page 2
#original-page(595.2pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(275.323pt, 91.92pt, "Abstract")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90pt, 123.12pt, "Thermal and structural characterizations of hybrid bonding structures are essential for ")
  #line-at(90pt, 154.32pt, "understanding heat transport in three-dimensional integrated circuits (3D-ICs). In this ")
  #line-at(90pt, 185.52pt, "work, we investigate the effective thermal conductivity of the Cu/dielectric HB layer ")
  #line-at(90pt, 216.72pt, "using time-domain thermoreflectance (TDTR) combined with picosecond ultrasonic ")
  #line-at(90pt, 247.92pt, "technique. Shallow-angle polishing enabled depth-resolved thermal measurements by ")
  #line-at(90pt, 279.12pt, "exposing hybrid bonding layers with different remaining thicknesses, while acoustic ")
  #line-at(90pt, 310.32pt, "echoes were used to identify buried interfaces and determine the thickness. The distinct ")
  #line-at(90pt, 341.52pt, "waveform of the bonding interface echo compared with the Cu/dielectric interface echo ")
  #line-at(90pt, 372.72pt, "suggests that its acoustic response may also reflect the interfacial bonding conditions. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 403.92pt, "The extracted thermal conductivity ranges from 1.14 to 1.75 W∙m")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(407.905pt, 399.84pt, "-1")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(414.57pt, 403.92pt, "∙K")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(426.236pt, 399.84pt, "-1")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(432.9pt, 403.92pt, " for the bottom ")
  #line-at(90pt, 435.12pt, "pad layer and from 1.76 to 4.34 W∙m")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(279.281pt, 431.04pt, "-1")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(285.946pt, 435.12pt, "∙K")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(297.612pt, 431.04pt, "-1")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(304.276pt, 435.12pt, " for the top pad layer. The difference in ")
  #line-at(90pt, 466.32pt, "thermal conductivity is consistent with the different Cu area fractions of the two layers. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 497.52pt, "Furthermore, the thermal conductivity of the top pad layer increases significantly with ")
  #line-at(90pt, 528.72pt, "the remaining thickness, possibly due to the thermal boundary resistance at the bonding ")
  #line-at(90pt, 559.92pt, "interface, low thermal conductivity of SiCN interlayer, and increased electron scattering ")
  #line-at(90pt, 591.12pt, "in thin Cu structures. Our work demonstrates a practical approach to investigate the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 622.32pt, "thermal properties of buried hybrid bonding layers, providing experimental data for ")
  #line-at(90pt, 653.52pt, "thermal design and modeling of 3D-ICs. ")
]

// arXiv source page 3
#original-page(595.2pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(259.086pt, 91.92pt, "1. Introduction ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90pt, 123.12pt, "The rapid growth of high-performance computing (HPC) and artificial intelligence (AI) ")
  #line-at(90pt, 154.32pt, "has driven increasing demand for high integration density and improved system ")
  #line-at(90pt, 185.52pt, "performance. As transistor scaling approaches its physical limits, three-dimensional ")
  #line-at(90pt, 216.72pt, "integrated circuits (3D-ICs) have emerged as a promising approach for sustaining ")
  #line-at(90pt, 247.92pt, "performance improvement [1]. Among the key technologies for 3D-ICs, hybrid bonding ")
  #line-at(90pt, 279.12pt, "enables finer interconnect pitches than conventional micro-bumps, with reported pitch ")
  #line-at(90pt, 310.32pt, "scaling below 10 μm and towards submicrometer scale [2][3][4]. Therefore, hybrid ")
  #line-at(90pt, 341.52pt, "bonding has been widely adopted in various applications, including CMOS image ")
  #line-at(90pt, 372.72pt, "sensors, high bandwidth memory (HBM), 3D NAND, and 3D V-cache [5][6][7]. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 435.12pt, "Hybrid bonding has been reported to improve power delivery and signal routing by ")
  #line-at(90pt, 466.32pt, "replacing micro-bumps with densely aligned Cu/dielectric interconnects, which provide ")
  #line-at(90pt, 497.52pt, "fine-pitch connections and enable inter-tier metal sharing [8][9][10]. Beyond electrical ")
  #line-at(90pt, 528.72pt, "advantages, the thermal properties of hybrid bonding layers are also critical as the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 559.92pt, "power density of 3D-ICs continues to increase. Hybrid bonding is expected to provide ")
  #line-at(90pt, 591.12pt, "low thermal resistance by replacing solder and underfill with a thin Cu/dielectric ")
  #line-at(90pt, 622.32pt, "bonding layer [11][12][13]. Bulk copper has an intrinsic thermal conductivity of ")
  #line-at(90pt, 653.52pt, "approximately 400 W∙m")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(210.876pt, 649.44pt, "-1")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(217.541pt, 653.52pt, "∙K")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(229.207pt, 649.44pt, "-1")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(235.871pt, 653.52pt, ", which is much higher than that of typical solder or ")
  #line-at(90pt, 684.72pt, "polymer underfill materials [14][15].  ")
]

// arXiv source page 4
#original-page(595.2pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90pt, 91.92pt, "Several simulation studies have evaluated the effective thermal conductivity of hybrid ")
  #line-at(90pt, 123.12pt, "bonding layers based on Cu/dielectric finite element model and incorporated it into ")
  #line-at(90pt, 154.32pt, "package-level simulations [16][17]. However, as the Cu feature size continues to shrink, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 185.52pt, "size effects and thermal boundary resistance can increasingly affect the thermal ")
  #line-at(90pt, 216.72pt, "properties of hybrid bonding layers [18][19][20]. Experimental studies have also ")
  #line-at(90pt, 247.92pt, "characterized thermal transport in hybrid bonding structures, including the effective ")
  #line-at(90pt, 279.12pt, "thermal properties of bonded layers and the thermal conductivity of individual Cu pads ")
  #line-at(90pt, 310.32pt, "[21][22][23][24]. However, the Cu pad dimensions can differ between the upper and ")
  #line-at(90pt, 341.52pt, "lower bonding layers, potentially leading to variations in thermal transport across ")
  #line-at(90pt, 372.72pt, "hybrid bonding structures. More detailed thermal characterization is therefore needed ")
  #line-at(90pt, 403.92pt, "to understand the depth-dependent thermal properties and provide reliable inputs for ")
  #line-at(90pt, 435.12pt, "thermal design and modeling of related devices and packaging. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 497.52pt, "In this study, we employed time-domain thermoreflectance (TDTR) for depth-resolved ")
  #line-at(90pt, 528.72pt, "thermal characterization of hybrid bonding layers. Shallow-angle polishing of the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 559.92pt, "sample enabled measurements at different remaining thicknesses, while picosecond ")
  #line-at(90pt, 591.12pt, "acoustic echoes identified the bottom pad/dielectric and top/bottom pad interfaces. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 622.32pt, "Separate layer and equivalent layer models were then used in TDTR fitting to evaluate ")
  #line-at(90pt, 653.52pt, "the thermal conductivities of the individual pad layers and the equivalent hybrid ")
  #line-at(90pt, 684.72pt, "bonding layer, respectively. ")
]

